	(text "The ADXL345 datasheet recommends that for the\nlowest-noise performance, it be powered with 2.5V\n- and the cleanest power possible. However, this might\nbe overkill and unnecessary, even for ADXL-based\nnozzle probing. So you can bypass this with R13 instead."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.472 137.668 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1aade7d7-0204-41b4-ac8f-460bd5266094")
	)
	(text "POWER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 138.43 36.576 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7b595187-b0b7-4b74-a957-a92fa5b25ef1")
	)
	(text "LP5907 regulators are\nanother good choice for these two.\nLow noise is the aim."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.566 103.378 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "d64c3202-dce5-48b9-af26-8d598aa25b45")
	)
	(text "The 3 fans, depending on model,\nwill draw a total of about 0.6A\nfrom the 5V supply\n- if they are 5V-powered.\n\nMCU seems to draw max 23mA,\nand the ADXL only 140uA, so\nthese can be disregarded.\nSo, the max draw from\nthe 5V supply will be about 0.6A,\nor 3W.\n\nAnd then for the 24V supply to the board,\nincluding 40W heater and 0.3A extruder motor,\nwhole board should draw about 2.1A max."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 92.71 109.982 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e80c0f03-756d-4ed0-867b-2f6d6689dae7")
	)
